# netsurf: name lookup off the main thread for the curl fetcher
# Generated 2026-09-23
#
# Hardware run 11: vitaSDK's libcurl has no asynchronous resolver (its
# asyn-thrdd object is empty), so curl looked names up with a blocking
# getaddrinfo() inside curl_multi_perform(), on the browser's only thread.
# A DNS server that did not answer froze everything for curl's 30 s
# connect timeout, per page.
# - content/fetchers/curl_resolve.h (new): fetch_curl_resolve(), a lookup
#   that never blocks, implemented by the frontend (WITH_CURL_ASYNC_RESOLVE).
# - curl.c: start() asks it first. PENDING: the job stays queued (start()
#   returns false, as it already does "inside cURL") and fetch_kick is
#   scheduled to retry in 50 ms. READY: the address goes to curl with
#   CURLOPT_RESOLVE, so curl never resolves by itself. FAILED: the fetch
#   never reaches curl and ends on the next poll through fetch_curl_done()
#   with CURLE_COULDNT_RESOLVE_HOST -- the error curl itself would give.
# - content/fetch.c/.h: fetch_kick(), fetch_start()'s dispatch-and-poll
#   step as a schedule callback (fetch_pump() dispatches but does not
#   restart the poll chain, so a deferred job could be stranded).
# - vita/resolve.c/.h (new): one worker thread, lookups one at a time,
#   each bounded (sceNetResolverStartNtoa, 2 s x 2 tries); a 32-entry
#   cache (answers 5 min, failures 15 s); lines for the log handed to the
#   main loop (vita_resolve_poll). In the simulator, getaddrinfo(); names
#   ending .sim-hang take the Vita's worst case and fail, standing in for
#   a DNS server that never answers.
# - vita/Makefile: resolve.c, -DWITH_CURL_ASYNC_RESOLVE.
# See docs/phase-0/10-hardware-test-plan.md §Run 12.

